  "notes": "{整形|せいけい} has two related but distinct meanings, both involving reshaping or correcting the body.\n\nSENSE 1 - COSMETIC SURGERY:\nRefers to surgery performed to improve appearance. Often used casually to mean 'getting work done.'\n- ⟦{美容|びよう}→美容：00014_biyou⟧{整形|せいけい} (cosmetic/aesthetic surgery)\n- {整形|せいけい}⟦{手術|しゅじゅつ}→手術：03218_shujutsu⟧ (plastic surgery operation)\n- {整形|せいけい}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧ (to have plastic surgery)\n\nSENSE 2 - ORTHOPEDICS:\nRefers to the medical treatment of bones, joints, and muscles.\n- {整形|せいけい}{外科|げか} (orthopedic surgery department)\n- {整形|せいけい}⟦{外科医|げかい}→外科医：21001_gekai⟧ (orthopedic surgeon)\n\nDISAMBIGUATION:\nIn casual conversation, {整形|せいけい} alone usually implies cosmetic surgery. For orthopedics, the full compound {整形|せいけい}{外科|げか} is typically used. Context usually clarifies the intended meaning.",
